@h1 Document genres h1@

Every real document is a combination of the features in this section. This page
maps a few common genres to the handful of features that carry each one, with a
skeleton you can start from. Think of it as the bridge between learning the
pieces and building a whole thing.

@h2 Essay or article h2@

The everyday genre: flowing prose, headings for structure, an epigraph to set the
tone, maybe a table or a figure, and a works-cited list at the end. It leans on
prose, headings, a block quotation, a table, a figure, and a numbered list.

@@@pre
@h1 On Attention h1@

@blockquote
"Attention is the rarest and purest form of generosity." — Simone Weil
blockquote@

Opening paragraph that states the argument…

@h2 The evidence h2@

Body prose, with a figure where it helps.

@figure
@img |src ./chart.svg| |size medium|
@figcaption Figure 1. The trend over a decade. figcaption@
figure@

@h2 Works cited h2@

@ol
@li Weil, Simone. _Gravity and Grace_. Routledge, 1952. li@
ol@
pre@@@

@h2 Thesis or long-form h2@

A book-length work wants to be split across files, share a vocabulary, and
accumulate a bibliography. It leans on multi-file assembly, a shared schema and
source list, and block-form chapter wrappers pulled together by a master file —
see @a |href /docs/write/multi-file/| Multi-file manuscripts a@ and
@a |href /docs/write/citations/| Citations & references a@.

@@@pre
reference ./shared/sources.wit

#chapter_one
@h2 Chapter One h2@

The opening of the argument…
chapter_one#
pre@@@

@h2 Data report h2@

A report built from live data: a roster, a table of figures, a chart, laid out
in columns. It leans on a load node feeding tables and figures, arranged with
rows and columns — see @a |href /docs/write/rendering/| Rendering a@ and
@a |href /docs/write/layout/| Layout a@.

@@@pre
@h1 Quarterly Report h1@

@table |schema [platform, downloads]| |rows @downloads|

@row
@col |size 300|
@figure @img |src ./chart.svg| |size full| figure@
col@
@col
The headline: macOS led this cycle, with Windows close behind.
col@
row@
pre@@@

@h2 Letter h2@

A short, personal genre: a title block with hard line breaks, a date, a
salutation, the body, and a sign-off. It leans on prose, the line break, and
plain headings.

@@@pre
Ada Lovelace @br br@
12 Analytical Way @br br@
London

4 July 2026

Dear Mr Babbage,

The engine's behaviour on the second card puzzles me…

Yours faithfully, @br br@
Ada
pre@@@

@aside(class note) 💡 An honest note: a few genre examples floating around the
project's skill files point at sample documents that do not exist in this
repository. Treat any such example as a _shape_ to imitate, and build your own
version to confirm it works before relying on it. aside@

